<title>UK: EBRD loans $23.2 mln for Lithuania roads.</title>
<headline>EBRD loans $23.2 mln for Lithuania roads.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Bank for Reconstruction and Development (EBRD) is to provide a $23.2 million loan to develop Lithuania's road system.</p>
<p>The EBRD loan, along with funds provided by other co-financiers, will be used to improve Lithuania's road infrastructure as well as to create job opportunities in road-side service and construction sectors, EBRD first vice president Ron Freeman said in a statement.</p>
<p>Lithuania needs to improve the Via Baltica highway, which links it to the other Baltic states and Europe, and the East-West highway which runs from the Belarus border to the port of Klaipeda.</p>
<p>The EBRD loan has a 15 year term, including a four year grace period and is part of a $117.1 million project co-financed by the Export-Import Bank of Japan, the European Investment Bank, the Nordic Investment Bank and is subsidised by the European Union's PHARE programme.</p>
<p>The loan is EBRD's second road project in Lithuania.</p>
<p>-- David Chance, London newsroom 44 171 542 5887</p>
